// Blizzard's map frame OpenMap hosts in (`WorldMapFrame`), and the game's tooltip beside a pin, as `worldMap.lua`
// reads them: the frame isn't declared by the client's API. Nothing is written to it: its scripts are hooked.
import Client from "$client"

// The world map's canvas, where pins stand; nil before Blizzard's map is made.
public function canvas(): any Client::Frame | nil
// The map the world map shows (`WorldMapFrame:GetMapID()`); 0 while it doesn't show.
public function shownMap(): Integer
// `run` is called when the world map shows or hides and when the map it shows changes. Once; `forget` takes it away.
// `run` is also called as the map's side panel shows, hides or changes size.
public function listen(run: () => nil)
// The map's side panel (`WorldMapFrame.QuestLog`, Blizzard's quest log) while it shows, and its width and height in
// UI units; nil and 0 while it doesn't.
public function sidePanel(): (any Client::Frame | nil, Number, Number)
public function forget()
// Blizzard's quest marks on its map (its quest pins and the shaded area of the map's focused quest) of `quest` alone:
// the quest shown on the map, its area drawn; 0 for every quest's, as the game has them.
public function onlyQuest(quest: Integer)
// The game's tooltip beside a pin: its first line the title, in white, the others under it.
public function tip(owner: any Client::Frame, lines: Array<String>)
public function untip()
// Ordaen's section of a dungeon's card in OpenMap (`RegisterDungeonSection`): `run` is given the dungeon's map and its
// instances' names, and gives the section's title then its lines, or none for no section. `noDungeonSection` takes it
// off.
public function dungeonSection(run: (map: Integer, names: Array<String>) => Array<String>)
public function noDungeonSection()
// OpenMap's townsfolk from QuestieDB's NPCs and objects (`RegisterTownsfolkProvider`), each zone's map by its area
// from `maps`; called where QuestieDB holds contract 4. `noTownsfolk` takes them off.
public function townsfolk(maps: Map<Integer, Integer>)
public function noTownsfolk()
